\subsection{Lexical ranking}

The lexical ranker scores a passage by how much of the claim's vocabulary it
contains.
We tokenize both claim and passage into informative lowercase words---dropping
stopwords and single characters, which carry no topical signal---and score by
the fraction of the claim's tokens that the passage covers.

This is a recall-oriented score on purpose: a passage that mentions most of the
claim's terms should surface even when it phrases them differently, because the
human (or the LLM re-ranker) makes the final call.
It is also free and deterministic, which is exactly what the classifier wants
for a cheap per-paper prefilter.

<<quote extraction constants>>=
# Function words carry no topical signal, so we ignore them when measuring
# overlap between a claim and a passage.
STOPWORDS = frozenset({
    "the", "a", "an", "and", "or", "but", "if", "then", "of", "to", "in",
    "on", "for", "with", "as", "by", "at", "from", "that", "this", "these",
    "those", "is", "are", "was", "were", "be", "been", "being", "it", "its",
    "we", "our", "they", "their", "can", "may", "also", "such", "which",
    "than", "into", "via", "using", "used", "not", "no",
})

_WORD_RE = re.compile(r"[a-z0-9]+")
@

<<quote extraction functions>>=
def _tokenize(text: str) -> set[str]:
    """Return the set of informative lowercase word tokens in ``text``."""
    return {
        token
        for token in _WORD_RE.findall(text.lower())
        if len(token) > 1 and token not in STOPWORDS
    }


def rank_passages_lexical(
    claim: str,
    passages: list[Passage],
    limit: int,
) -> list[QuoteCandidate]:
    """Rank passages by lexical overlap with the claim.

    The score is the fraction of the claim's informative tokens present in
    the passage, so passages covering more of the claim's vocabulary rank
    higher. Passages with no overlap are dropped.

    Args:
        claim: The claim to find support for.
        passages: Candidate passages.
        limit: Maximum number of candidates to return.

    Returns:
        Up to ``limit`` candidates, highest score first.
    """
    claim_tokens = _tokenize(claim)
    if not claim_tokens:
        return []
    scored: list[QuoteCandidate] = []
    for passage in passages:
        overlap = claim_tokens & _tokenize(passage.text)
        if overlap:
            scored.append(
                QuoteCandidate(
                    page=passage.page,
                    text=passage.text,
                    score=len(overlap) / len(claim_tokens),
                )
            )
    scored.sort(key=lambda candidate: candidate.score, reverse=True)
    return scored[:limit]
@

